# Schedule only: the engines the build would take for its link streams in the
# report too (a cost model prices the schedule as built); the page columns are
# laid out with the copies, so only streams are listed.
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkhbm
# RUN: foldsim --srcs top.f --top Top --out %t/so --static --nest --modulo --page 1 --storage Unit:pages=hbm,Reader:pages=hbm --page-engines auto --link-kinds Unit:Reader:hbm,Reader:Unit:hbm --schedule-only Unit Reader > %t/so.log 2>&1
# RUN: FileCheck %s --check-prefix=SO < %t/so/schedule.txt
# SO: page engines: 2 engines, 0 page columns
# SO-NEXT: page engine 0 32 bits, tag 7, row 6: link:Reader>Unit
# SO-NEXT: page engine 1 32 bits, tag 7, row 6: link:Unit>Reader
# Streams of words not whole bytes (29 bits): an engine's row is whole bytes,
# its byte mask covering the stream's row (the stream alone on an engine was
# 29 bits under a 3-bit mask, its top bits never written; the compiler
# stopped building the mask).
# RUN: cd %S/../Driver/Inputs/linkodd
